From: gennro <gennro2004@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] soc: cix: dst: bound boot_record()'s copy into its event buffer

boot_record() copied strlen(str) bytes into the fixed event[BOOT_STR_SIZE]
of the next log slot without a bound check, so a long initcall name (or a
string written to /proc) overran into the next slot, and with
FORTIFY_SOURCE the copy traps. It also tested boot_log_count before taking
the lock that guards it, so two callers could both take the last slot.

Copy with strscpy_pad(), which bounds the copy to the buffer and keeps it
NUL-terminated, and test the count under the lock.

Kettle Linux (Radxa Orion O6N).
---
 drivers/soc/cix/cix_dst/hw_boottime.c | 11 +++++------
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+), 6 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/soc/cix/cix_dst/hw_boottime.c b/drivers/soc/cix/cix_dst/hw_boottime.c
index 84172d725..a0c5d69cb 100755
--- a/drivers/soc/cix/cix_dst/hw_boottime.c
+++ b/drivers/soc/cix/cix_dst/hw_boottime.c
@@ -112,17 +112,16 @@ void boot_record(const char *str)
 	if (hw_boottime_enabled == 0)
 		return;
 
+	if (strncmp(BOOTUP_DONE, str, strlen(BOOTUP_DONE)) == 0)
+		hw_boottime_enabled = 0; // zygote start
+	mutex_lock(&hw_boottime_lock);
 	if (boot_log_count >= BOOT_LOG_NUM) {
+		mutex_unlock(&hw_boottime_lock);
 		DST_PN("[boottime] no enough boottime buffer\n");
 		return;
 	}
-	if (strncmp(BOOTUP_DONE, str, strlen(BOOTUP_DONE)) == 0)
-		hw_boottime_enabled = 0; // zygote start
-	mutex_lock(&hw_boottime_lock);
 	hw_boottime[boot_log_count].time_us = sky1_get_time_us();
-	memset(&hw_boottime[boot_log_count].event, 0,
-	       sizeof(hw_boottime[boot_log_count].event));
-	memcpy(&hw_boottime[boot_log_count].event, str, strlen(str));
+	strscpy_pad(hw_boottime[boot_log_count].event, str);
 
 	boot_log_count++;
 	mutex_unlock(&hw_boottime_lock);
